llm_gen_dict:
   The Academy Awards in 1972 recognized the film with wins in the Best Picture, Best Director, Best Actor, Best Adapted Screenplay, and Film Editing categories, with nominees in the Best Supporting Actor, Best Cinematography, and Best Sound categories. The film was also recognized at the American Cinema Editors and BAFTA awards, winning Best Film Editing and Best Actor awards, respectively. The film won the David di Donatello Award for Best Foreign Film and the Directors Guild of America Award for Outstanding Directorial Achievement. Additionally, the film received nominations at the Edgar Allan Poe Awards, Golden Globe Awards, Kansas City Film Critics Circle, National Society of Film Critics, New York Film Critics Circle, and Writers Guild of America. 
