Row 0:{Category: Growth factors, or mitogens,Examples: c-Sis,Cancers: glioblastomas, fibrosarcomas, osteosarcomas, breast carcinomas, and melanomas,Gene functions: induces cell proliferation.}
Row 1:{Category: Receptor tyrosine kinases,Examples: epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR), platelet-derived growth factor receptor (PDGFR), and vascular endothelial growth factor receptor (VEGFR), HER2/neu,Cancers: Breast cancer, gastrointestinal stromal tumours, non-small-cell lung cancer and pancreatic cancer,Gene functions: transduce signals for cell growth and differentiation.}
Row 2:{Category: Cytoplasmic tyrosine kinases,Examples: Src-family, Syk-ZAP-70 family, and BTK family of tyrosine kinases, the Abl gene in CML - Philadelphia chromosome,Cancers: colorectal and breast cancers, melanomas, ovarian cancers, gastric cancers, head and neck cancers, pancreatice cancer, lung cancer, brain cancers, and blood cancers,Gene functions: mediate the responses to, and the activation receptors of cell proliferation, migration, differentiation, and survival}
Row 3:{Category: Cytoplasmic Serine/threonine kinases and their regulatory subunits,Examples: Raf kinase, and cyclin-dependent kinases (through overexpression).,Cancers: malignant melanoma, papillary thyroid cancer, colorectal cancer, and ovarian cancer,Gene functions: Involved in organism development, cell cycle regulation, cell proliferation, differentiation, cells survival, and apoptosis}
Row 4:{Category: Regulatory GTPases,Examples: Ras protein,Cancers: adenocarcinomas of the pancreas and colon, thyroid tumors, and myeloid leukemia,Gene functions: involved in signalling a major pathway leading to cell proliferation.}
Row 5:{Category: Transcription factors,Examples: myc gene,Cancers: malignant T-cell lymphomas and acute myleoid leukemias, breast cancer, pancreatic cancer, retinoblastoma, and small cell lung cancer,Gene functions: -They regulate transcription of genes that induce cell proliferation.}

