Row 6:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Henry E. Bodurtha Highway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 5.0,Location: Agawam,Notes: Freeway comprises the eastern 5 miles (8.0 km) of Route 57, connecting Route 187 to U.S. Route 5 and I-91.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 7:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Boston-Worcester Turnpike,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): ,Location: Worcester to Boston,Notes: Route 9 between Worcester and Boston is mostly a divided full-access highway with traffic light-controlled intersections which serves as one of the main alternatives to the Massachusetts Turnpike. Many shopping centers, car dealers, full-service restaurants and businesses line the roadway on this stretch, especially in Framingham, such as Barnes & Noble, Marshalls, T.G.I. Fridays, Kohl's, Toys "R" Us, Best Buy, Olive Garden and Walmart. This stretch of the roadway is also encompassed in the Golden Triangle district of Massachusetts.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 8:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Central Artery (John F. Fitzgerald Expressway),Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 3.18,Location: Boston,Notes: The Central Artery is the portion of I-93 in downtown Boston, which runs from Massachusetts Ave. (just south of Exit 20) north to U.S. Route 1's departure at Exit 27. Route 3 leaves the Artery at Exit 26.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 9:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Commonwealth Avenue,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): ,Location: Newton, Boston,Notes: Stretches from Weston/Newton line to the Boston Public Garden.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 10:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: East Boston Expressway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 1.2,Location: Boston,Notes: The East Boston Expressway comprises the first 1.2 miles (1.9 km) of Route 1A's northern segment. It stretches from I-93 Exit 24 at the southern end of the Callahan Tunnel (northbound) and the Sumner Tunnel (southbound) to just northeast of the interchange with Route 145 in East Boston, near the eastern end of the Mass Pike.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 11:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Grand Army of the Republic Highway,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 117.46,Location: Seekonk to Provincetown,Notes: The cross-country U.S. Route 6 is designated Grand Army of the Republic Highway over its entire length, which spans 3,205 miles (5,158 km).,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 12:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Horseneck Beach Connector,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 13.03,Location: Westport,Notes: Route 88 serves as a connector running from the Horseneck Beach Reservation north to I-195 Exit 10 in Westport.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 13:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Loop Connector,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 3.56,Location: Methuen,Notes: Route 213 is designated "Loop Connector." It serves as a freeway connection between Interstates 93 and 495 in Methuen.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 14:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Lydia Taft Highway,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 3,Location: Uxbridge,Notes: Route 146A in Massachusetts is designated as the Lydia Taft Highway, which runs from the Rhode Island state border to Route 122 in Uxbridge.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 15:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Massachusetts Turnpike,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 138.1,Location: West Stockbridge to Boston,Notes: The Mass Pike is a toll road running from the New York state border to downtown Boston. It serves as the main cross-state freeway connecting the western and eastern portions of the state. The "Pike" carries the easternmost 138 miles (222 km) of cross-country Interstate 90.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 16:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Memorial Drive,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 4.12,Location: Cambridge,Notes: U.S. Route 3 and MA Route 3 connect to each other on Memorial Drive, which runs from the Fresh Pond Parkway to Main Street. Route 2 travels along Memorial Drive with US-3 and leaves via the Boston University Bridge.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 17:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Mid-Cape Highway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 36.6,Location: Bourne to Orleans,Notes: The Mid-Cape Highway is the main highway on Cape Cod, a 36-mile (58 km) long freeway running from Route 3 and the Sagamore Bridge east to the Orleans Rotary.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 18:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Mohawk Trail,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 65,Location: Williamstown to Orange,Notes: The 65-mile (105 km) Mohawk Trail comprises the western section of Route 2, from the New York border east to Orange, and is regarded as one of the most scenic drives in the area.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 19:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Mystic Valley Parkway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): ,Location: Arlington, Medford, Winchester,Notes: Runs from the Alewife Brook Parkway to the Revere Beach Parkway.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 20:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Northeast Expressway,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 4.1,Location: Boston, Chelsea, Revere,Notes: This section of U.S. Route 1 runs from I-93 Exit 27 (Tobin Bridge) to an interchange with Route 60 in Revere. This was originally supposed to be part of I-95, but I-95 was cancelled in Boston, with I-93 and US-1 taking its place.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 21:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Northwest Expressway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 21.1,Location: Burlington to Tyngsborough,Notes: The Northwest Expressway serves as a freeway connection between I-95/Route 128 (Exit 32A) in Burlington and the F.E. Everett Turnpike in Nashua, NH.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 22:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Pilgrims Highway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 42.5,Location: Bourne to Braintree,Notes: The Pilgrims Highway is the southern portion of Route 3, a 42-mile (68 km) long freeway which serves as a connector between Cape Cod (via U.S. Route 6) and the Boston metropolitan area (via I-93 and I-95).,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 23:{Unnamed: 0: - U.S. Route 44 runs along the highway between Exits 6 and 7.,Name: nan,Route number(s): None,Length (mi): None,Location: None,Notes: None,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 24:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Southeast Expressway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): ,Location: Braintree to Boston,Notes: The Southeast Expressway is the section of I-93 between the Route 3 split (Exit 7) and the Mass Ave. interchange (Exit 18), where it continues into Boston as the Central Artery.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 25:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Southern Artery,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 2.13,Location: Quincy,Notes: The Southern Artery is a major arterial in the city of Quincy, running from Quincy Ave to the Furnace Brook Parkway.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 26:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Taunton-New Bedford Expressway (Alfred M. Bessette Memorial Highway),Route number(s): ,Length (mi): 19.3,Location: New Bedford to Taunton,Notes: The New Bedford Expressway comprises the southern 19 miles (31 km) of Route 140, and serves as a freeway connection between U.S. Route 6 in New Bedford and Route 24 (Exit 12) in Taunton, near I-495.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 27:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Ted Williams Highway,Route number(s): ,Length (mi): ,Location: Framingham,Notes: Route 9 in Framingham is named the Ted Williams Highway, in commemoration of late Boston Red Sox Hall-of-Famer Ted Williams who wore the number 9 on his jersey.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 28:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Wilbur Cross Highway,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 8.0,Location: Sturbridge,Notes: I-84 in Massachusetts is designated the Wilbur Cross Highway. It runs 8 miles (13 km) from the Connecticut state border to the Mass Pike at Exit 9.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 29:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Name: Worcester-Providence Turnpike,Route number(s): *,Length (mi): 20.99,Location: Millville to Worcester,Notes: Route 146 is a freeway that, along with Rhode Island's Route 146, serves to connect the metropolitan areas of Providence and Worcester. The entire route starts from I-95 in Providence, with the Massachusetts section picking up at the state line in Millville. The highway runs 21 miles (34 km) northward, intersecting the Mass Pike (I-90) in Worcester, and terminating at I-290 shortly thereafter.,Unnamed: 6: nan}
