Row 1:{Common name: Arjun,Binomial nomenclature: Terminalia arjuna Terminalia elliptica,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: 870 kg/m³,Location: Central India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is heavy and strong. It has such uses as beams, rafters, and posts.}
Row 2:{Common name: Axlewood,Binomial nomenclature: Anogeissus latifolia,Colour: nan,Density ¹: 930 kg/m³,Location: Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Bihar, Uttar Pradesh,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is very strong, hard and tough. It takes a smooth finish. It is subject to cracking.}
Row 3:{Common name: Babul,Binomial nomenclature: Acacia nilotica subsp. indica,Colour: Whitish red,Density ¹: 835 kg/m³,Location: Rajasthan, Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Bengal, Gujarat, Uttar Pradesh,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong, hard and tough and it takes up a good polish. It is used for such products as bodies and wheels of bullock cart, agricultural instruments, tool handles, and well curbs.}
Row 4:{Common name: Bakul,Binomial nomenclature: Mimusops elengi Mimusops parvifolia,Colour: Reddish brown,Density ¹: 880 kg/m³,Location: Some parts of North India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is close-grained and tough. It is used for making cabinets.}
Row 5:{Common name: Bamboo,Binomial nomenclature: Family Poaceae, tribe Bambuseae,Colour: nan,Density ¹: nan,Location: Throughout India, especially Assam and Bengal,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Not actually a tree, but a woody grass, it is flexible, very strong and durable. It is used for scaffoldings, thatched roofs, rafters, temporary bridges, and so forth.}
Row 6:{Common name: Banyan,Binomial nomenclature: Ficus benghalensis,Colour: Brown,Density ¹: 580 kg/m³,Location: Throughout India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong and durable only under water. The aerial roots are utilized for such items as tent poles and well curbs.}
Row 7:{Common name: Benteak,Binomial nomenclature: Lagerstoemia parviflora,Colour: nan,Density ¹: 675 kg/m³,Location: Kerala, Madras, Maharashtra, Karnataka,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong and takes up a smooth surface. It may be used for building constructions, boat building and furniture.}
Row 8:{Common name: Bijasal,Binomial nomenclature: Pterocarpus marsupium,Colour: Light brown,Density ¹: 800 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Kerala, Uttar Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Orissa,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is coarse-grained, durable and strong but difficult to work. Termites (also known as white ant) do not easily attack it. It is used for ordinary building construction and for cart wheels. Vulnerable}
Row 9:{Common name: Casuarina,Binomial nomenclature: Casuarina spp.,Colour: Reddish brown,Density ¹: 765 kg/m³,Location: Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It grows straight. It is strong and fibrous. It is, however, badly twisted. It is often used for scaffolding and posts for temporary structures.}
Row 10:{Common name: Coconut,Binomial nomenclature: Cocos nucifera,Colour: Reddish brown,Density ¹: nan,Location: Throughout coastal India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Takes polish. Requires preservative treatment. Used as poles, piles, furniture and as formwork in concrete construction.}
Row 11:{Common name: Deodar,Binomial nomenclature: Cedrus deodara,Colour: Yellowish brown,Density ¹: 560 kg/m³,Location: Himalayas, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Deodar is the most important timber tree providing soft wood. It can be easily worked and it is moderately strong. It possesses distinct annual rings. It is used for making cheap furniture, railway carriages, railway sleepers, packing boxes, structural work and so forth.}
Row 12:{Common name: Gambar,Binomial nomenclature: Gmelina arborea,Colour: Pale yellow,Density ¹: 580 kg/m³,Location: Central India, South India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It can be easily worked and is strong and durable especially when used under water. It is used for such products as furniture, carriage, well curbs, yokes, and door panels.}
Row 13:{Common name: Hopea,Binomial nomenclature: Hopea parviflora,Colour: Light to deep brown,Density ¹: 1010 kg/m³,Location: Madras, Kerala,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Hopea is extremely strong and tough. It is difficult to work. However, it can be seasoned easily and it is durable and not likely to be damaged by white ants. It has been variously used for ordinary house construction, railway sleepers, piles, and boat building. Endangered}
Row 14:{Common name: Himalayan Elm, Indian Elm,Binomial nomenclature: Ulmus wallichiana,Colour: Red,Density ¹: 960 kg/m³,Location: Throughout India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is moderately hard and strong. It is used for door and window frames, carts, and so forth.}
Row 15:{Common name: Ironwood, Penaga Lilin,
Bosneak, Gangaw, Mesua,Binomial nomenclature: Mesua ferrea,Colour: Reddish brown,Density ¹: 960–1060 kg/m³,Location: nan,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Ironwood is durable though it is very hard and is not easily worked. It even resists penetration of nails. It is used for ordinary house construction, bridges, piles, agricultural instruments, railway wagons, and railway sleepers.}
Row 16:{Common name: Irul, Pyinkado,Binomial nomenclature: Xylia xylocarpa,Colour: nan,Density ¹: 830–1060 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Kerala, Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra, Orissa, Tamil Nadu,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is very hard, heavy and durable. Difficult to work, it also requires slow and careful seasoning. It is used for railway sleepers, agricultural instruments, paving blocks, and heavy construction. Least concern}
Row 17:{Common name: Jack,Binomial nomenclature: Mangifera caesia.,Colour: Yellow, darkens with age,Density ¹: 595 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu, Kerala,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is compact and even grained. It is moderately strong and easy to work. It takes a good finish and maintains its shape well. It has many uses including plain furniture, boat construction, well curbs, door panels, cabinet making and musical instruments.}
Row 18:{Common name: Jarul,Binomial nomenclature: Lagerstroemia flos-reginae,Colour: Light reddish gray,Density ¹: 640 kg/m³,Location: Assam, Bengal, Maharashtra,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Hard and durable, it can be easily worked. It takes a good finish and is used for house construction, boat building, railway carriages, cart making and scaffolding.}
Row 19:{Common name: Kathal, Keledang, Jackfruit,Binomial nomenclature: Artocarpus heterophyllus,Colour: Yellow to deep brown,Density ¹: 800 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Kerala, Maharashtra, Tamil Nadu,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is heavy and hard. It is durable under water and in damp conditions, however, it cracks if exposed to direct sun. White ants do not attack it. It is used for piles, platforms of wooden bridges, door and window panels.}
Row 20:{Common name: Lauraceae, Saj,Binomial nomenclature: Lauraceae,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: 880 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Orissa, Madhya Pradesh, Kerala, Tamil Nadu,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong, hard and tough. It is subject to cracking and attack by dry rot. White ants do not attack it. It takes a smooth finish. It is used for such purposes as house construction, boat construction, railway sleepers and structural work.}
Row 21:{Common name: Mahogany,Binomial nomenclature: Swietenia spp.,Colour: Reddish brown,Density ¹: 720 kg/m³,Location: nan,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It takes a good polish and is easily worked. It is durable under water. It is most commonly used for furniture, pattern making and cabinet work.}
Row 22:{Common name: Mango,Binomial nomenclature: Mangifera spp,Colour: Deep gray,Density ¹: 560–720 kg/m³,Location: Throughout India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: The mango tree is well known for its fruits. It is easy to work and it maintains its shape well. It is moderately strong. It is most often used for cheap furniture, toys, packing boxes, cabinet work, panels for doors and for windows.}
Row 23:{Common name: Mulberry,Binomial nomenclature: Morus spp.,Colour: Brown,Density ¹: 650 kg/m³,Location: Punjab,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong, tough and elastic. It takes up a clean finish. It can be well seasoned. It is turned and carved easily. Mulberry is typically used for baskets and sports goods like hockey sticks, tennis rackets and cricket bats.}
Row 24:{Common name: Oak,Binomial nomenclature: Quercus spp.,Colour: Yellowish brown,Density ¹: 865 kg/m³,Location: nan,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Oak is strong and durable, with straight silvery grain. It is used for preparing sporting goods.}
Row 25:{Common name: Palm,Binomial nomenclature: Arecaceae,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: 1040 kg/m³,Location: Throughout India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It contains ripe wood in the outer crust. The colour of this ripened wood is dark brown. It is strong, durable and fibrous. Palm is used for furniture, roof covering, rafters and joists.}
Row 26:{Common name: Pine,Binomial nomenclature: Pinus spp.,Colour: nan,Density ¹: nan,Location: nan,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Pine wood is hard and tough except white pine which is soft. It decays easily if it comes into contact with soil. It is heavy and coarse grained. It is used for pattern making, frames for doors and windows, and for paving material. White pine is light and straight grained and is used in the manufacture of matches.}
Row 27:{Common name: Red cedar,Binomial nomenclature: nan,Colour: Red,Density ¹: 480 kg/m³,Location: Assam, Nagpur,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is soft and even grained. It is used for furniture, door panels and well curbs.}
Row 28:{Common name: Rosewood,Binomial nomenclature: Dalbergia latifolia,Colour: Dark,Density ¹: 850 kg/m³,Location: Kerala, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Orrissa,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is strong, tough and close-grained. It is a handsome wood that takes up a high polish. It maintains its shape well and is available in large sizes. It is used for furniture of superior quality, cabinet work, ornamental carvings and so forth. Vulnerable}
Row 29:{Common name: Sal,Binomial nomenclature: Shorea robusta,Colour: Brown,Density ¹: 880–1050 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Madhya Pradesh, Orissa,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is hard, fibrous and close-grained. It does not take up a good polish. It requires slow and careful seasoning. It is durable under ground and water. It is used for railway sleepers, shipbuilding, and bridges.}
Row 30:{Common name: Sandalwood,Binomial nomenclature: Santalum spp.,Colour: White or Red,Density ¹: 930 kg/m³,Location: Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Assam, Nagpur, Bengal,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It has a pleasant smell. It is commonly used for agricultural instruments, well curbs, wheels, and mallets. Vulnerable}
Row 31:{Common name: Satinwood,Binomial nomenclature: Chloroxylon swietenia,Colour: Yellow,Density ¹: 960 kg/m³,Location: Central and Southern India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is very hard and durable. It is close grained. It is used for furniture and other ornamental works. Vulnerable}
Row 32:{Common name: Simul,Binomial nomenclature: Bombax spp.,Colour: White,Density ¹: 450 kg/m³,Location: All over India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is a loose grained, inferior quality wood. Light in weight, it is used for packing cases, the match industry, well curbs, and for cheap furniture.}
Row 33:{Common name: Siris,Binomial nomenclature: Albizia spp.,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: nan,Location: North India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Hard and durable, Siris wood is difficult to work. It is used for well curbs in salty water, beams, posts, and furniture.}
Row 34:{Common name: Sissoo,Binomial nomenclature: Dalbergia sissoo,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: 770 kg/m³,Location: Mysore, Maharashtra, Assam, Bengal, Uttar Pradesh, Orissa,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Also known as shisham or tali, this wood is strong and tough. It is durable and handsome and it maintains its shape well. It can be easily seasoned. It is difficult to work but it takes a fine polish. It is used for high quality furniture, plywoods, bridge piles, sport goods, railway sleepers and so forth. It is a very good material for decorative works and carvings.}
Row 35:{Common name: Spruce,Binomial nomenclature: Picea spp.,Colour: nan,Density ¹: 480 kg/m³,Location: nan,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Spruce wood resists decay and is not affected by the attack of marine borers. It is however liable to shrink, twist and warp. It is used for piles under water and (formerly) for aeroplane construction.}
Row 36:{Common name: Sundri,Binomial nomenclature: Heritiera fomes,Colour: Dark red,Density ¹: 960 kg/m³,Location: Bengal,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It is hard and tough. It is difficult to season and work. It is elastic and close grained. It is strong and durable. These qualities make it suited for such uses as boat building, piles, poles, tool handles, and carriage shafts.}
Row 37:{Common name: Tamarind,Binomial nomenclature: Tamarindus indica,Colour: Dark brown,Density ¹: 1280 kg/m³[citation needed],Location: All over India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Tamarind is knotty and durable. It is a beautiful tree for avenue and gardens. Its development is very slow but it ultimately forms a massive appearance. Its fruit is also very useful. It is used for agricultural instruments, well curbs, sugar mills, carts and brick burning.}
Row 38:{Common name: Teak,Binomial nomenclature: Tectona grandis,Colour: Deep yellow to dark brown,Density ¹: 639 kg/m³,Location: Central India and Southern India,Characteristics, Usage and Status: Moderately hard, teak is durable and fire-resistant. It can be easily seasoned and worked. It takes up a good polish and is not attacked by white ants and dry rot. It does not corrode iron fastenings and it shrinks little. It is among the most valuable timber trees of the world and its use is limited to superior work only.}
Row 39:{Common name: Toon, Red Cedar,Binomial nomenclature: Toona ciliata,Colour: Reddish brown or dull red,Density ¹: 450 kg/m³,Location: Assam,Characteristics, Usage and Status: It can be easily worked. It is light in weight. It is used for such products as furniture, packing boxes, cabinet making and door panels.}

Row 0:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 1,Prod #: 2,Title: Menace Of The Mole Men,Summary: The Fantastic Four are off to carry out their experiments on a remote island. The Mole Man, however, has been waiting for them and traps them in a radiation field and plans to submerge the world’s largest cities. The Fantastic Four escape but the Mole Man traps them again. They manage to escape their separate ways. They foil Mole Man’s domination and escape the island once and for all.,Air Date: 9/9/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 1:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 2,Prod #: 3,Title: Diablo,Summary: The Fantastic Four find a ruined castle in the middle of a forest in Transylvania. Ben is summoned by Diablo and unable to resist, opens Diablo's prison, unleashing him and later brainwashing Ben. Diablo tricks the world into thinking he has the power to help them. The world then realises what a fraud Diablo really is. The Fantastic Four seize this opportunity to attack Diablo’s castle. After getting far in the dungeons, the four get captured. Ben escapes, releases the others and they defeat Diablo.,Air Date: 9/16/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 2:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 3,Prod #: 7,Title: The Way It All Began,Summary: While on a television show, Reed recalls the time he first met Victor von Doom before he became Dr. Doom. He had Ben as his roommate at university. Victor was working on dangerous experiments, especially a test that brought him to the hospital and got him expelled from university. Worse than that, the test altered his face and he swore revenge on Reed having to hide his work from him. Ben and Reed became soldiers in World War II. Ben, Susan, Johnny and Reed all went aboard a space rocket for space exploration. And so the origin of the Fantastic Four began. Dr. Doom confronts the Fantastic Four on the television show and briefs them on his origin. After that Dr. Doom attempts to get his revenge, but fails and escapes only to crash.,Air Date: 9/23/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 3:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 4,Prod #: 5,Title: Invasion Of The Super-Skrull,Summary: The Skrulls have immediately failed to destroy the Fantastic Four. They introduce The Super-Skrull who possesses double power effects the Fantastic Four have. The Fantastic Four are overwhelmed by the Super-Skrull’s combined powers. The Fantastic Four lure the Super-Skrull to Crater Island. Susan plants a sonic wave jamming device on the Super-Skrull before he can destroy them with his ultimate power level.,Air Date: 9/30/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 4:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 5a,Prod #: 1,Title: Klaws,Summary: Klaw is here to vanquish the Fantastic 4 with his solidifying sonic waves. Johnny is on vacation or so it would seem and arrives in the nick of time to assist Mr. Fantastic in catching The Klaw.,Air Date: 10/7/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 5:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 5b,Prod #: 4,Title: The Red Ghost,Summary: Reed is competing with Dr. Kragoff in race to the moon for astronomical research. During the launch, Dr. Kragoff and his primate crew have developed some reverse energy powers. Dr. Kragoff is now transparent and becomes the Red Ghost. Red Ghost kidnaps Susan after counter attacking. She escapes and thwarts Red Ghost’s attempt to eliminate her companions. Using a special device, Reed turns Red Ghost into a plastic statue.,Air Date: 10/7/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 6:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 6,Prod #: 9,Title: Prisoners Of Planet X,Summary: A UFO has been sighted. The pilot abducts the Fantastic Four from the Science Center and is setting course for Planet X. There, their dictator Kurrgo requests the Fantastic Four save their planet from another planet knocked off its orbit. Reed manages to formulate a working plan to save the population. While the plan is in process, Kurrgo has other ideas. However, Reed tricks Kurrgo and leaves him on the exploding planet while the micro-sized population and the Fantastic Four get away to safety.,Air Date: 10/14/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 7:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 7,Prod #: 14,Title: It Started On Yancy Street,Summary: The Fantastic Four face a bunch of old rivals in Yancy Street, but their old enemy Red Ghost and his primates show up and capture them. During their voyage to the moon, the four turn the tables, but Red Ghost gets away and the four are dumped on the moon. They barely manage to get to a source of oxygen which is the Watcher’s laboratory. Using one of the Watcher’s machines, Reed brings down Red Ghost’s ship. Susan gets Dr. Kragoff banished into a trans-nitron machine. Reed uses that machine to get back to Earth.,Air Date: 10/21/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 8:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 8,Prod #: 6,Title: Three Predictions Of Dr. Doom,Summary: Dr. Doom challenges the Fantastic Four. Doctor Doom begins his plans by capturing Susan. Soon the Fantastic Four manage to locate and penetrate Dr. Doom’s flying fortress, but Ben is turned back to his former self and the other three are trapped. Ben turns himself back into the Thing, releases the others and aborts Dr. Doom’s tidal waves. They chase Dr. Doom out and back to the flying fortress. After a struggle through the dangerous complex of the fortress, they abort Dr. Doom’s global destruction for good.,Air Date: 10/28/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 9:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 9,Prod #: 8,Title: Behold A Distant Star,Summary: The Fantastic Four are testing their rocket when they are drawn into the Skrull Galaxy. After beating the first round of Skrulls, the Fantastic Four weaken and are taken prisoner. The cruel Skrull Warlord Morrat wishes to overthrow the Skrull Emperor. The Warlord gives the Fantastic Four the option to assist them or die. Reed tricks the Warlord into getting him and his friends' powers fully charged. They defeat the Warlord as the Emperor arrives and he allows the Fantastic 4 to go freely back to Earth.,Air Date: 11/4/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 10:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 10,Prod #: 12,Title: Demon in the Deep,Summary: The Fantastic Four beat the criminal forces working for Dr. Gamma, and blow up the island with its secret weapons. While escaping, Dr. Gamma is infected by the radiation levels in the seabed and morphs into some creature. Johnny is flustered with being moved around and quits from the Fantastic Four. In the town Johnny goes to, there have been sightings of the Gamma Ray. Johnny defeats the Gamma Ray by himself, but he comes back with the hideous giant sea monster Giganto. Johnny rejoins the Fantastic Four. Ben succeeds in eliminating the sea monster. The Gamma Ray is defeated but not finished.,Air Date: 11/11/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 11:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 11,Prod #: 11,Title: Danger In The Depths,Summary: Johnny finds a mysterious lady named Lady Dorma and takes her back to the Headquarters. She claims to have come from a land beneath the sea called Pacifica, which is under siege by Attuma. They manage to slip past Attuma’s forces. Pacifica is losing hope and Attuma has shadowed the seabed. Triton can only fight man-to-man with Attuma while his men prepare traps to weaken Triton into a losing battle. The Fantastic 4 thwart every trap. Triton beats Attuma and the forces retreat. NOTE: Due to the rights to the Sub-Mariner being held by Grantray-Lawrence Animation, the adaptation of the first meeting between the FF and Namor was altered. Instead, Prince Triton, an original pastiche of Namor was reworked into the Namor role.,Air Date: 11/18/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 12:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 12,Prod #: 13,Title: Return Of the Mole Man,Summary: The Mole Man is creating earthquakes and causing buildings to sink deep into the Earth. In addition, he and his Moloids kidnap Susan. The Mole Man as usual has been expecting the other three and sends them back to the surface to tell the Army not to get involved. They manage to halt them and seek an alternate entrance in the underworld. Johnny rescues Susan, then they penetrate the laboratory. They all return the buildings to the surface and escape the exploding caves.,Air Date: 11/25/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 13:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 13,Prod #: 19,Title: Rama-Tut,Summary: After coming back from vacation Reed tells Ben an interesting theory on attempting to restore him. They head to Dr. Doom’s deserted castle to use the time machine the doctor left behind. In 2000 B.C the four weaken during a fight and are taken by Pharaoh Rama-Tut, who is a lot more than he would seem at first sight. Susan is to be Rama-Tut’s queen while the other three are put to work with some mind control. Ben turns back to his former self. As he rescues Susan, he is once again the Thing. The four battle Rama-Tut to his sphinx. Finally, they destroy his sphinx and return to their own time.,Air Date: 12/9/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 14:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 14,Prod #: 15,Title: Galactus,Summary: The Watcher has made strange events in hope of preventing the Silver Surfer from coming but the plan fails and the Surfer summons Galactus. Susan assists the unconscious Surfer and he begins to think differently. The Watcher has a plan only Johnny can undergo. Reed and Ben sabotage Galactus' Earth draining machine and the Silver Surfer arrives to battle Galactus. This angers Galactus, but Johnny gets back with the weapon that makes Galactus see reason not to destroy the Earth. NOTE: In the episode "Galactus", Susan Richards (The Invisible Girl) has the role originated by Alicia Masters (explaining to the Silver Surfer about humanity).,Air Date: 12/16/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 15:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 15,Prod #: 16,Title: The Micro World Of Dr. Doom,Summary: The Fantastic Four have been shrunken to small size. Dr. Doom is after them and takes them to the Micro World. Dr. Doom briefs them on his micro genius experiments involving a king and a princess from the micro world. The four battle the giant guards but Dr. Doom catches them and imprisons them with the King and Princess. They all escape and enlarge themselves. Ben puts a stop to the Lizard Men, then the four return to their own world.,Air Date: 12/30/1967,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 16:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 16,Prod #: 17,Title: Blastaar, The Living Bomb-Burst,Summary: On a remote planet, its inhabitants are fighting against Blastaar and are able to banish him. Reed and Johnny enter the dangerous space zone via dimensional transport. As they depart, Blastaar escapes and follows them. Blastaar is too powerful for the four to handle. They lure Blastaar into an evacuated atomic power plant, where they use some atomic matter to put him in a coma. They eject him through the dimensional transport back into the space zone.,Air Date: 1/6/1968,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 17:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 17,Prod #: 10,Title: The Mysterious Molecule Man,Summary: The Fantastic Four study a radiated meteor. The Molecule Man appears and threatens the public. After the Fantastic Four tastes some of his power, he leaves to undergo his ruling the world. Reed has developed a weapon he thinks will defeat the Molecule Man. The weapon works, but the Molecule Man gets away. The Fantastic Four continue their pursuit. The plan to stop the Molecule Man is tricky. They manage to reverse the Molecule Man’s form with a fragment of the meteor.,Air Date: 1/13/1968,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 18:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 18,Prod #: 18,Title: The Terrible Tribunal,Summary: The Fantastic Four are taken to another planet where they are regarded as criminals against evil, charged by three old enemies. Reed is forced to recall his memories on Klaw, Molecule, Man and Blastaar’s defeat. Meanwhile the other three escape and they rescue Reed just as the verdict is given. At the surface, they have to battle the court judge before they are able to leave the planet for Earth.,Air Date: 9/14/1968,Unnamed: 6: nan}
Row 19:{Unnamed: 0: nan,Eps #: 19,Prod #: 20,Title: The Deadly Director,Summary: The Imposter plans to lure the Fantastic Four into a trap by posing as a famous Hollywood director. The four are tempted to be in a movie and briefly retell their previous adventures to the director. The next day, the four fly to the director’s island and the director blows them out of the sky. The Fantastic Four are forced to go through the director’s deadly movie landscapes and make it to the boat on the other side of the island which the director detonates. The Imposter removes his disguise and the Fantastic Four surprise him. The real director prevents the Imposter from escaping upon forgetting that he had locked the director in the room that Imposter was escaping into. The Fantastic Four have no desire to be movie stars in the end.,Air Date: 9/21/1968,Unnamed: 6: nan}

