Row 0:{Speed: 202.6 km/h (126 mph),Date: 1938-07-03,Country: UK,Train: LNER Class A4 No. 4468 Mallard,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unkn.,Comments: Downhill grade. Data indicates peak speed 202.6 km/h (126 mph), mean speed (half-mile) 201.2 km/h (125 mph). Mallard suffered an overheated crankpin during the run, but was repaired and returned to traffic within 9 days.}
Row 1:{Speed: 200.4 km/h (125 mph),Date: 1936-05-11,Country: Germany,Train: Borsig DRG series 05 002,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unkn.,Comments: Level grade.[citation needed]}
Row 2:{Speed: 185.07 km/h (115 mph),Date: 1905-06-11,Country: USA,Train: Pennsylvania Railroad E2 #7002,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unmod.,Comments: Claimed.[by whom?] Clocked at Crestline, Ohio at 127.1 mph (205 km/h) in 1905. However PRR Steam Locomotives did not carry speedometers at that time, speed was calculated by measuring time between mile markers, so this is not recognized as a speed record.[citation needed]}
Row 3:{Speed: 182.4 km/h (113 mph),Date: 1972-10-11,Country: Germany,Train: BR 18 201,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unkn.,Comments: The fastest operational steam locomotive as of 2011.[citation needed]}
Row 4:{Speed: 181.1 km/h (113 mph),Date: 1935-04-05,Country: USA,Train: Milwaukee Road class A #2,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unkn.,Comments: Claimed[by whom?] to have sustained 112.5 mph (181 km/h) for 14 miles (23 km). Average speed for 136 miles (219 km) between Milwaukee and New Lisbon, Wisconsin was 74.9 mph (121 km/h).}
Row 5:{Speed: 180.3 km/h (112 mph),Date: 1935-09-29,Country: UK,Train: LNER Class A4 2509 Silver Link,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unkn.,Comments: Authenticated. Some sources say 112.5 mph.[citation needed]}
Row 6:{Speed: 168.5 km/h (105 mph),Date: 1935-03-05,Country: UK,Train: LNER Class A3 No. 2750 Papyrus,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unmod.,Comments: First run at 100+ mph with complete, surviving documentation.[citation needed]}
Row 7:{Speed: 166.6 km/h (104 mph),Date: 1934-07-20,Country: USA,Train: Milwaukee Road class F6 #6402,Arr.: Loc,Power: Steam,State: Unmod,Comments: A point between Oakwood, Illinois and Lake, Wisconsin. Also averaged 75.5 mph (122 km/h) on 85 miles (137 km) from Chicago, Illinois to Milwaukee, and 89.92 mph (145 km/h) for a 68.9 miles (110.9 km) stretch}
