Row 9:{Nation: Canada,Date: 2009,Quantity: 9.0,Type: 4207,Notes: In 2009 the Department of Fisheries and Oceans announced it would be purchasing 9 patrol vessels for the Canadian Coast Guard. The Hero-class patrol vessels began entering service in 2011.}
Row 10:{Nation: Mexico,Date: 2012,Quantity: 6.0,Type: 4207,Notes: The Mexican Navy – Armada de México – inducted the first two of what could be several Tenochtitlan-class coastal patrol boats.[citation needed] The two StanPatrol 4207 patrol boats – ARM Tenochtitlan (PC-331) and ARM Teotihuacan (PC-332) were built at a cost of $9 million USD each at ASTIMAR 1 in Tampico, Tamaulipas and completed in April and May 2012.}
Row 11:{Nation: United States,Date: 2012,Quantity: nan,Type: 4708,Notes: The United States Coast Guard is proposing the purchase of 24-34 cutters as the Sentinel class.}
Row 12:{Nation: Bulgaria,Date: 2010,Quantity: 1.0,Type: 4207,Notes: The Bulgarian Border Police accepted delivery of the Obzor on July 16, 2010.}
Row 13:{Nation: Venezuela,Date: 2014,Quantity: 6.0,Type: 4207,Notes: The Bolivarian Armada of Venezuela ordered 6 vessels together with 6 Damen Ocean Patrol 5007 in March 2014. They are being built in UCOCAR shipyard with the assistance of DAMEX Shipbuilding & Engineering, Cuba.}
Row 14:{Nation: Venezuela,Date: 2014,Quantity: 6.0,Type: 5009,Notes: The Bolivarian Armada of Venezuela ordered 6 vessels together with 6 Damen Stan Patrol 4207 in March 2014. They are being built in UCOCAR shipyard with the assistance of DAMEX Shipbuilding & Engineering, Cuba.}
