Row 0:{Town name: White Cloud,County: Doniphan County,Established: 1856,Disestablished: ,Current Status: 2008 estimated population of 227,Remarks: }
Row 1:{Town name: Ray,County: Pawnee County,Established: ,Disestablished: ,Current Status: Most of the houses were demolished or moved in the 1950s. The old Co-op remains and still bears the town name. Large berm south of the co-op is what is left from the demolition 38.174742,-98.962701,Remarks: }
Row 2:{Town name: Iowa Point,County: Doniphan County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: Post Office closed in 1933,Current Status: Small population near K-7,Remarks: }
Row 3:{Town name: Eagle Springs,County: Doniphan County,Established: 1883,Disestablished: ,Current Status: Townsite was abandoned, only ruins remain,Remarks: Was a health resort that lasted into the 1930s.}
Row 4:{Town name: Geary City,County: Doniphan County,Established: March 23, 1856,Disestablished: ,Current Status: Only foundations remain,Remarks: }
Row 5:{Town name: Doniphan,County: Doniphan County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: 1943,Current Status: Still on maps but little remains,Remarks: A trading post was established on the site in 1852}
Row 6:{Town name: Four Houses,County: Wyandotte County,Established: ,Disestablished: ,Current Status: Exact location unknown,Remarks: Was actually a trading post from 1826-1828}
Row 7:{Town name: Rising Sun,County: Jefferson County,Established: 1857,Disestablished: mid-1860s,Current Status: A Kansas River access point is near the location and named after the town.,Remarks: Was a Lecompton satellite community.}
Row 8:{Town name: Hickory Point,County: Jefferson County,Established: 1855,Disestablished: ,Current Status: A Kansas State Historical Marker is near the location along U.S. 59.,Remarks: Location of the Battle of Hickory Point, a skirmish between pro-slavery and free state forces.}
Row 9:{Town name: Arrington,County: Atchison County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: ,Current Status: A small population resides along K-116.,Remarks: }
Row 10:{Town name: Kennekuk,County: Atchison County,Established: 1858,Disestablished: ,Current Status: ,Remarks: }
Row 11:{Town name: America City,County: Nemaha County,Established: February 14, 1857,Disestablished: Post office closed in 1933,Current Status: A couple buildings and a cemetery remain,Remarks: }
Row 12:{Town name: Juniata,County: Pottawatomie County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: 1858,Current Status: On private property and not accessible,Remarks: }
Row 13:{Town name: Pawnee,County: Riley County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: 1855,Current Status: The old territorial capitol building still stands is well-preserved,Remarks: Was the territorial capitol until 1855 when it was moved to Shawnee Mission.}
Row 14:{Town name: Randolph,County: Riley County,Established: 1855,Disestablished: ,Current Status: 2008 estimated population of 198,Remarks: Moved two miles west when Tuttle Creek Lake was built.}
Row 15:{Town name: Irving,County: Marshall County,Established: 1859,Disestablished: 1960,Current Status: Located on Corps land and is easily accessible.,Remarks: Abandoned for the construction of Tuttle Creek Lake.}
Row 16:{Town name: Alcove Springs,County: Marshall County,Established: ,Disestablished: ,Current Status: Now a well-preserved park,Remarks: Was never an official town but was a stop on the Oregon Trail. Numerous carvings in the spring's rocks feature traveler's initials and other things. A member of the Donner Party is buried nearby.}
Row 17:{Town name: Trading Post,County: Linn County,Established: 1842 (established as a trading post),Disestablished: ,Current Status: A small population remains just off of U.S. 69.,Remarks: Near the site of the Marais des Cygnes massacre.}
Row 18:{Town name: Centropolis,County: Franklin County.,Established: 1854,Disestablished: 1930,Current Status: A small population remains on a county road about ten miles northwest of Ottawa Centropolis Christian Church and Centropolis Baptist Church are open.,Remarks: }
Row 19:{Town name: Minneola,County: Franklin County,Established: 1854,Disestablished: 1860s,Current Status: Nothing remains of the town.,Remarks: Was the territorial capitol briefly in 1858. Not to be confused with Minneola in Clark County.}
Row 20:{Town name: Silkville,County: Franklin County,Established: 1870,Disestablished: 1892,Current Status: Several buildings remain including an old house and a stone school southwest of Williamsburg.,Remarks: }
Row 21:{Town name: Black Jack,County: Douglas County,Established: 1857 (incorporated),Disestablished: 1870s,Current Status: Santa Fe Trail wagon swales, a roadside park, cemetery and the well-preserved battlefield site remain and are open to public.,Remarks: }
